# Crystal Imperium play test: EASY CATCH (challenge menu > Features, ON by default).
# A wild Route 29 Pokemon is given Mewtwo's catch rate (3) by setting its battle species, so a
# normal Poke Ball at full HP catches it about 1.5% of the time. With EASY CATCH ON the first
# ball catches; with it OFF two balls fail. R in the action menu throws the last-used ball.
# The wild battler's species is gBattleMons+136.

# EASY CATCH ON (default)
!new_game()
!give_mon(155, 5)
!give_item(1, 5)
!warp(0, 11, 0)
!walkto(34, 14, "yx")
!walkto(24, 14, soft=True)
!pace(21, 25, 14, 10, soft=True)
expect32 {gMain+4} {BattleMainCB2+1} wild_battle_on
wait 300
press A
wait 300
poke16 {gBattleMons+136} 150
press R
wait 600
shot 01_easy_catch_on.png
# "Gotcha!", catch EXP (large: the species reads as Mewtwo), then the nickname prompt; B
# advances the text and answers No
wait 400
mash B 2400
shot 02_after_catch.png
expect8 {gPlayerPartyCount} 2 first_ball_caught_it

# EASY CATCH OFF
reset
!new_game(easy_catch=False)
!give_mon(155, 5)
!give_item(1, 5)
!warp(0, 11, 0)
!walkto(34, 14, "yx")
!walkto(24, 14, soft=True)
!pace(21, 25, 14, 10, soft=True)
expect32 {gMain+4} {BattleMainCB2+1} wild_battle_off
wait 300
press A
wait 300
poke16 {gBattleMons+136} 150
press R
wait 900
shot 03_easy_catch_off_throw1.png
mash B 120
poke16 {gBattleMons+136} 150
press R
wait 900
shot 04_easy_catch_off_throw2.png
expect32 {gMain+4} {BattleMainCB2+1} still_battling_after_two_balls
expect8 {gPlayerPartyCount} 1 nothing_caught_without_easy_catch
